A||N||19||WhiteFieroBlur||Should we hate the Rice?||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||10-24-2001||01:30 AM||||I know what rice is but I was wondering is it really all that bad. I know alot of you really hate these cars and all. I for one love a nice looking lowered honda, eclipse, supra, or whatever car with a full body kit and nice looking spoiler with rims. I think its a very beautiful car. Now I am not all for them saying cause it looks fast that its all fast and can beat any car. So should we really hate the rice or just not like the people who drive the rice? I also get kinda mad and jelous about how cheap they can get a kit but we have to spend thousands on a kit. Well it was just my opinion, I am kinda confused about the rice bashing, when I first came here, I was like whats all this talk about rice? But since I know now, I still think rice is not a bad thing at all. Just maybe the people who take it too far. and go that step further that makes you hate the car cause of a wild paint job or what not.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jefrysuko||10-24-2001||01:50 AM||||I don't appreciate the mentality of most of them.  Of course the main thing I am talking about is how some of them think a body kit or stickers makes them faster.  I actually had one ask me once when I was going to do something to make my car faster.  Since he hadn't seen anything but the outside of my car I asked "how do you know that I haven't" to which he responded, "Well you don't have any stickers or body mods.  Then you have the guys that take some sort of a Geo and put on a coffee can, a huge wing and blue bottle in the car and think it is hell on wheels and still running 15 sec 1/4 mile times.<P>Now I do have a friend who is quite different than your typical ricer.  He is running a CRX si and the car looks and sounds completely stock unless he winds it up.  He swapped in some sort of later model motor and turbo charged it.  He doesn't have a coffee can in fact he has had a hard time finding an exhaust system that would actually make his car quieter.  He runs mid 13's and drives it daily.  This is the type of guy that I respect and don't consider him a "ricer" even though he drives a Honda.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||10-24-2001||01:52 AM||||I think "rice" is one of those descriptives that is so widely overused that it has become  stoopid. When I think of riced I think of the Civic DX or Neon 4 door riding on 13" stock wheels with a big ol Supra wing and Pep Boyz coffee can on the tailpipe. Not thoughtfully modded cars with the tuner look to them. I was at a car show where there were some kind imports there with extreme paint, wheels, stereo. Put these things on a Fiero like FST2M6 does and everyone drools (myself included) but put them on an Eclipse or Maxima and people disrespect. Sad really.||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||10-24-2001||02:45 AM||||Fear leads to anger, anger leads to hate, hate leads to.... suffering!!!<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||TRiAD||10-24-2001||09:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Fear leads to anger, anger leads to hate, hate leads to.... suffering!!!<BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>YODA!<P>OK...Rice IS:<BR>1)stickers on a car for products/companies that are NOT associated with it. (Type R mustangs, for instance)<BR>2)Non-performance items installed to add performance, or the illusion thereof. (painted 2 liter bottles that look like N02 bottles...)<BR>3)any other serious contradiction of visual appearance and actual performance. <P>RICE is NOT:<BR>1) any car with something on it "you" don't like (or understand). <BR>2) any car with large wings or graphics.<BR>3) any FWD car with a rear wing<BR>4) any sport-compact or import with ANY modification done to it. <P>--------<P>So, according to this thread, you don't mind seeing the occasional Type R sticker on a mustang, toyota, or other non-Type R car. That's fine. <BR>Either that or you simply thought rice was BIG graphics and semi-tasteless bodykits. That's fine too. <P>Laters!<P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||10-24-2001||09:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B> <BR>OK...Rice IS:<P>...painted 2 liter bottles that look like N02 bottles...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR><I>Please</I> tell me you are joking. Have you seen somebody actually do this?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||10-24-2001||10:20 AM||||Good description of what rice is, and isn't.<P>I also like import cars that have had a lot of work put into them.  I think rice is as much the attitude of the owner than the mods themselves.  He tends to be a punk a$$ kid with a bunch of cheap (costing and looking) mods stuck to a relatively cheap car and he thinks he is better than everyone else on the road because of it.  Thats the rice I do not care for.||||reg||1
Z||000007||WhiteFieroBlur||10-24-2001||10:38 AM||||ok so we hate the guy with the fake car with fake stickers and stuff? I see those cars sometimes but we don't have people who do that here. The cars I see are the cars that look just like the movie in fast and furious wth the street fighter kits and blitz kits and shogun kits with the spoilers that they have in the movies. So are these cars considered rice? I mean they have no stickers on them or anything, maybe ghost flames on the side painted on. And the people here who maybe have a NOS sticker actually to have NOS in them. I live in army town so you know how army guys get with hooking there cars up. Its like one big town with everyone competing to get the nicest car possible. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Philphine||10-24-2001||11:46 AM||||don't really know what rice is, not bothered with figuring it out. the way i play with cars it could be (probaly is) me. <P>it's something i kind of had a real problem with on another forum (warning: diatribe coming). i think the age group was older there more affluent (which was another reason i didn't belong there) and the people forgot about being young themselves. i can't believe they didn't put some unexplainable stuff on their cars when they were young. i mean, what do you need a racoon tail for? i guess none of them were the ones who had the back of the carjacked up with n50 15's on their cragars (or keystones in my case).<P> editing my self 'cause i could feel pages coming on. i guess i should just say if i like a car i like it and if i don't it's not mine anyway.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Hank is Here||10-24-2001||11:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WhiteFieroBlur:<BR><B>ok so we hate the guy with the fake car with fake stickers and stuff? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hate?  no just a strong dislike generally speaking for the attitude of the owners.  <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B> The cars I see are the cars that look just like the movie in fast and furious wth the street fighter kits and blitz kits and shogun kits with the spoilers that they have in the movies. So are these cars considered rice? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I just consider them ugly. If the car does not claim anything that it is clearly not then I have no issue with it.  Nothing wrong with these cars they just don't appeal to my tastes.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||GTFiero1||10-24-2001||03:40 PM||||rice doesnt just mean jap cars. i saw a dodge neon painted brith yellow with a gigantic rear spoiler...i mean this thing, if you take it off and set it next to the car, it would probably be as tall as it. the neon was proabably a 4cyl anyway. that wing was completely pointless. it looked so dumb. those twin turbos 300zx's or the 3000GT's (i actually like the 3000GTs) are actually fast and there real ment to be a sports car but when a guy takes his moms honda accord puts all sorts of scoops on it, the coffie can (theres some one up at pep boys who has a yellow beretta with one of these on it), a bunch of sticker i think its dumb. not everyone but all the ricers i met so far have nasty additudes toward american street machines. i belive if your born in america, live and work in america, than you should damn well drive american. we can get over 400hp out of a N/A small block chevy, the only way these ricers can get even close to 400hp is with 200 shots of nitrous and a couple of turbos. what i think is happening is that in the 70's when are car makers had problems with the gas shortege and emission laws, people started buyinh imports and noticed that the quality of the car was better, but the proplem is, they still think that, american cars are just as reliable and well built as jap cars. i haven't yet met a mechanic that owned an import....<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Return of Fiero||10-24-2001||04:30 PM||||i think rice comes down to more mentality and maturity. corect me if im wrong, but this also goes along with the bit prior about the "fake" items and stickers.<BR>the reasons i dislike what i belive to be "ricers"<BR>i have had a few of these boys pull up to me at a light when i dont have a customer in the car (mind you i own taxis in nashua but am in the process of changing jobs) and rev there puny engines. when the light turns green, i take off normal, and i hear them winding gears. we stay fairly even, and when i get tired of listening to the bee humming, i floor it and leave them in the dust. to me, if this was high performance, why does my 96' luminna eat up this "ricer" so easy? <BR>these stories i could tell all day, but i want to get the importaint one told. i had one of these guys pull up in his dropped crx, and do the norm and rev it up. as usual, i ignored him, and took off normal. when i got up set at listening to him,(about 20 mph usualy)i steped on it, the lumina dropped to first, and chirped. i shot off, and the sore losser decided i wasnt going to win without lossing somthing. this pri__ hit me on purpose. nice dent going dothe the passengers side of my once flawless taxi. this is where mentality comes in. this kid did it out of spite. he wasnt going to win, so he wanted no one to win. the maturity comes from them wanting to race all the time. (and no, im not racing them, i never get over the speed limit by more that 5mph) this imature attitude, and poor sportsmanship is what make them "ricers" its not in the car, it in the driver, i feel. (btw, i get dirty looks every time i roll donw central, where most these guys live. my taxi is quicker, and the sterio is clear/louder than i think all of them.<BR>Myke||||reg||1
Z||000012||Spektrum-87GT||10-24-2001||05:04 PM||||i dont understand why they spend so much money on making a slow economy car look fast. 300zx tt, supras, rx-7s with the ricer accessories... i dont hate. civics, integras, neons, the whole shibang of weak 4 bangers that people try to make look fast... disgusting. why spend so much to 'mod' a civic when you could have gotten a cobra or trans am for that price. go to a ricer event and ask them how much money it costed, and how fast it is... the average answer i've gotten is 40k, 14's. for 40k... you could have had one heck of a trans am that runs 10s, maybe 9s. in my opinion, the big word here is image, they try to put on a front and mold themselves and they're cars into the ricer image. they sure are fun to beat though! i've had many ricer kills already, never gets old!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Return of Fiero||10-24-2001||07:20 PM||||yeah, but he dented my car....:')<BR>(sob)<BR>i dont care about the immage, its the attitude that bugs me. i never have aproblem with them till they show the temperment they hold||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fierowrecker||10-24-2001||10:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B> YODA!<P>OK...Rice IS:<BR>1)stickers on a car for products/companies that are NOT associated with it. (Type R mustangs, for instance)<BR>2)Non-performance items installed to add performance, or the illusion thereof. (painted 2 liter bottles that look like N02 bottles...)<BR>3)any other serious contradiction of visual appearance and actual performance. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Would the opposite of rice be sleeper?<BR>NO stickers, graphics, or other HP advertisments...<BR>Perhaps a four door sedan instead of the two door coupe?<BR>A BIG but quiet (till matted) engine (460 HP)?<BR>NO scoops, bumps, flares, excessivly wide tires?<BR>Runs mid 13's in street trim including muffs?<BR>Sounds like my Nova...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000015||Simple Fiero||10-25-2001||03:51 PM||||I keep hearing everyone talking about 13's 14's 15's. Then you say trans ams, corbas, come on these civics and integras (especailly type-r) will run circles around, the big ass american cars on a track , and not strip, and not american circle jerk racing. I am talking Gt and touring tracks, with corners, and not just left turns right turns too. Oh yah and who won the Speedvision GT Series, oh yah it was a japanese car.( i believe) but I know that it wasn't a mustang or a corvette.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Slammed Fiero||10-25-2001||03:58 PM||||Wow , I frequent mosport and shannonville quite a bit and I have yet too see a prepped Honda beat a prepped F-Body. I mean Type R's are fast granted , and they are light. But even the best prepped cars at Mosport are seconds behind an F-Body with big bars and Race rubber.<P>Hp sells cars , TQ wins races.<P>Now at an autocross , yes a Honda that is prepped will dominate over a Big F -Body. But unfortunatley that changes a lot if you head out to a big track.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000017||danny boy||10-25-2001||05:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B> <BR> I think rice is as much the attitude of the owner than the mods themselves.  He tends to be a punk a$$ kid with a bunch of cheap (costing and looking) mods stuck to a relatively cheap car and he thinks he is better than everyone else on the road because of it. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is exactly what the word means.<P><BR>"Runs mid 13's in street trim including muffs?<BR>Sounds like my Nova..."<BR>HE,HE, mine does it in 11's W/ Cheater slicks. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Master_Sushi||10-25-2001||06:52 PM||||I think ricers are kind of funny. They never seem to bother me. Sometime I even point and laugh at them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!<BR>Its funny, I have a manual fan switch I put on my 84 coupe. Its next to the shifter, and its big and red... So I put a NOS sticker above it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Now this was ment completely as a joke, and most people think its funny. If I was seriously trying to trick people with it that would be somewhat rice like  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">.<P>Maybe I'll even try the blue painted bottle trick.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> hehe||||reg||10
Z||000019||Spektrum-87GT||10-25-2001||07:30 PM||||if you're hearing about modded f-body's or stangs, you should be hearing 8's 9's 10's. how many ricers do you know that take it to the track? gt racing != rice, i think they're a big misconception about what rice actually is... TRiAD explained it perfectly, just because you own a modded fwd import does not make you a ricer, owning a stickerfied, super wing, body kit, stock engine(cold air intake doesnt count) honda civic DOES make you a ricer. besides, barely any of them even race period, 'all show and no go', most admit it, but its fun to shut up the ones that think they're rice cooker actually is fast. Funniest thing i've ever seen was an 80s trans am stalking an 80's crx with the license plate 'later v8', needless to say the trans am embarresed him terribly at a light. the thing i've realized with ricer, the faster they look, the slower they are.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Simple Fiero:<BR><B>I keep hearing everyone talking about 13's 14's 15's. Then you say trans ams, corbas, come on these civics and integras (especailly type-r) will run circles around, the big ass american cars on a track , and not strip, and not american circle jerk racing. I am talking Gt and touring tracks, with corners, and not just left turns right turns too. Oh yah and who won the Speedvision GT Series, oh yah it was a japanese car.( i believe) but I know that it wasn't a mustang or a corvette.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
